__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.DS_Store
.venv/
config.json
# `trinity-local config --set` writes a .bak beside the config before every
# overwrite (that backup is what recovered the tree when a mutation run
# clobbered it). It is per-machine provider state and must never ship: two
# of them reached the public repo on 2026-09-08, one recording a provider
# disabled by a test.
config.json.bak
config.json.bak-*
state/
*.egg
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.Trinity Dispatch-signed.shortcut

# Session / dev artifacts — playwright traces, ad-hoc screenshots, agent state
.claude/
# ...EXCEPT the skill files, which are the method contract CLAUDE.md points at.
# Two were force-added years ago and stayed tracked (an ignore does not apply to
# an already-tracked file); council-review-plan was created later and silently
# was not, so the known-failure-modes list lived untracked and a fresh clone
# would not have carried it. Negating the directory ignore for this one path is
# what makes the omission impossible to repeat by accident.
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md
.claude.json
.playwright-mcp/
*.png
!docs/launchpad_example.png
!docs/favicon.png
!docs/og-card.png
!docs/launch_assets/*.png
!browser-extension/icons/*.png
!internal/launch-copy/*.png
mock_gen.py
pylint_report.txt

# Personal-data guard (the 2026-05-31 corpus leak): never commit machine-mined
# corpus briefs or raw ~/.trinity content. Enforcement is the docs/** PII grep in
# tests/test_doc_count_consistency.py; these patterns are belt-and-suspenders.
# Screenshots must be regenerated from a SYNTHETIC fixture, not ~/.trinity, so
# the smoke/me-card PNG re-include exceptions were removed above.
**/*corpus-gold*
**/preference_acts*.jsonl
conversations/

# Node.js artifacts — optional browser-extension smoke-test deps
node_modules/
browser-extension/package-lock.json
.agents/
launch_councils/
.antigravitycli/

# internal/ + docs/maxroom-redesign.html are intentionally version-controlled now
# (do NOT re-ignore them). Real personal data — config.json, conversations/,
# preference_acts*, *corpus-gold* — stays ignored above.

# memory bake-off bulk artifacts (2026-08-01): derived caches + per-arm retrieval
# dumps, ~235MB total, fully regenerable from prep_corpus.py + the arm scripts.
# The verdict artifacts (FINDINGS.md, score_summary.json, score_posthoc.json)
# and every .py instrument ARE committed.
internal/experiments/memory_bakeoff/*.npy
internal/experiments/memory_bakeoff/*.jsonl
internal/experiments/memory_bakeoff/results/retrieval_*.jsonl
internal/experiments/memory_bakeoff/results/retr_*.jsonl
internal/experiments/memory_bakeoff/*.npz

# GA4 ingestion credentials are injected into the WHEEL at publish time,
# never committed — this repo mirrors publicly.
src/trinity_local/_ga4_bundled.py

# Cross-agent handoff between the Claude and Codex sessions working this repo.
# Append-only JSONL, local coordination only, never published.
internal/agent_exchange/

# hq_113/114 packets and judge reads carry raw conversation text: local only
internal/experiments/hq113_packets*.jsonl
internal/experiments/hq114_reads.jsonl
internal/experiments/hq116_reads.jsonl
internal/experiments/hq117_labels.jsonl
internal/experiments/hq118_reads.jsonl
